{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Node 0 has large backlog and pipeline; increase order to clear backlog. Node 1 has inventory and pipeline; slightly increase to cover node 0's higher demand. Node 2 has low inventory; increase to replenish.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(6, backlog/10)"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory<20",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory<20",
          "delta": "3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Node 0: if backlog high, order more; else if pipeline low, order more. Node 1: if inventory low, order more. Node 2: if inventory low, order more.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>50",
          "delta": "4"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and pipeline<40",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory<15",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory<15",
          "delta": "4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Node 0: if backlog high, order more; else if pipeline low, order more. Node 1: if inventory low, order more. Node 2: if inventory low, order more.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>50",
          "delta": "4"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and pipeline<40",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory<15",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory<15",
          "delta": "4"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Moderate pipeline-aware relaxation: reduce node0 order when inventory is low and backlog exists, but only if pipeline is sufficient; node1 and node2 keep orders near recent demand to avoid starving downstream.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and inventory==0 and backlog>0 and pipeline>=20",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and inventory==0 and backlog>0 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog==0 and inventory>10",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Demand-responsive coordination: node0 orders up when recent demand exceeds baseline and pipeline is low; node1 orders up when its backlog is positive; node2 orders up when its backlog is positive and pipeline is low.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and growth>1.05 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and growth<0.95 and pipeline>40",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Backlog-clearing with pipeline awareness: node0 increases order when backlog is high and pipeline is low; node1 increases order when backlog is high; node2 increases order when backlog is high and pipeline is low; otherwise small reductions to avoid over-ordering.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>=5 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>=3",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>=3 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog==0 and inventory>10",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Pipeline-aware relaxation: reduce orders when pipeline is high relative to recent demand, and boost when backlog is high. Node0 has backlog 1 and pipeline 16, so reduce its order to avoid overstock; node1 has inventory 8 and pipeline 16, so reduce; node2 has no backlog and pipeline 16, so reduce. This prevents excess inventory and upstream backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "pipeline > 12 * recent",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "backlog > 0 and pipeline < 8 * recent",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "inventory > 10 and pipeline > 8 * recent",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "true",
          "delta": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Coordinated correction: node0 increases order to clear backlog and meet demand, while node1 and node2 reduce orders to avoid building inventory given ample pipeline. This balances downstream service and upstream cost.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 1 and inventory > 5",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 2 and pipeline > 10",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "true",
          "delta": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Demand-responsive: if recent demand exceeds baseline, increase orders to avoid stockouts; if pipeline is high, reduce orders to prevent overstock. Node0 has recent < baseline, so no increase; node1 and node2 have high pipeline, so reduce.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "recent > baseline and pipeline < 10 * recent",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "pipeline > 15 * recent",
          "delta": "-3"
        },
        {
          "when": "backlog > 0 and inventory == 0",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "true",
          "delta": "0"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Moderate demand-responsive increase at node0 to reduce backlog, with pipeline-aware caps at upstream nodes to avoid over-ordering.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(6, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog==0 and growth>1.1",
          "delta": "min(3, max(0, recent - baseline))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Aggressive backlog clearing at node0 and node1, but node2 orders only to maintain pipeline coverage, avoiding upstream backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(6, max(0, backlog - inventory + 2))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(5, max(0, backlog - inventory + 1))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "min(3, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog==0 and growth>1.2",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, recent - baseline))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Pipeline-aware relaxation: reduce orders when pipeline is high relative to recent demand, increase only when backlog exists and pipeline is low.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0 and pipeline < recent*4",
          "delta": "min(6, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0 and pipeline < recent*4",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0 and pipeline < recent*4",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, backlog - inventory))"
        },
        {
          "when": "pipeline > recent*6",
          "delta": "-2"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Refinement of llm_r0_2: keep its strong node0 backlog-clearing rule, but add a pipeline-aware relaxation for node0 when backlog is low and pipeline is high to avoid overloading node1. For node1, increase order when backlog is high and pipeline is not excessive, supporting node0 without starving node2. For node2, increase order when backlog is high and pipeline is low, but relax when pipeline is high to avoid upstream backlog. All corrections are small and bounded.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>=5 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog==0 and inventory>10 and pipeline>40",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>=3 and pipeline<60",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>=3 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Emergency demand may be hidden by low recent mean. Add small pipeline-aware safety orders at upstream nodes when their pipeline is empty and inventory is low, while keeping node0 near HAPPO to avoid extra downstream backlog. Node1 and node2 raise orders only if they have no incoming pipeline and low inventory, so they replenish before a possible surge without creating excess upstream backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0 and inventory<=2",
          "delta": "min(3, backlog)"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and pipeline==0 and inventory<=6",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and pipeline==0 and inventory<=8",
          "delta": "2"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
